// denext (DENEXT.md item 373): a process that signals itself with
// `process.kill(process.pid, sig)` (SIGTERM, SIGINT, SIGKILL) and has no
// listener for it ends, and with `--cpu-prof` it writes its profile first,
// as Node's at-exit work does. On Windows the process used to end at once
// (TerminateProcess), so no profile was written; a listener keeps Node's
// Windows rule (the process still ends, nothing is flushed).
{
  "tempDir": true,
  "args": "run -A main.mjs",
  "output": "main.out"
}
